   "search_text": "4. The  set Z(m, n)  consists  of  all  integers N  with mn  digits which\n  have  precisely n  ones, n  twos, n  threes,   . . ., n m s.   For each\n   integer N ∈Z(m, n), deﬁne d(N) to be the sum of the absolute values\n   of the diﬀerences  of  all pairs  of consecutive  digits.   For example,\n  122313 ∈Z(3, 2) with d(122313) = 1 + 0 + 1 + 2 + 2 = 6.  Find the\n  average value of d(N) as N ranges over all possible elements of Z(m, n).\n",
